{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966789,"nonce":"vMf8mRoSsYLpR7PTNtUMy2MkAxA=","title":"Lost clicks/drags when a rebuild fires between mouse-down and mouse-up — router state must","message":"EventRouter state that survives across event cycles MUST be keyed by\n`StableNodeId`, not `LayoutNodeId`. Slotmap version bumps after a\nrebuild invalidate any cached LayoutNodeId, and `dispatch_event_full`\nsilently drops events whose `tree.stable_id(node)` lookup returns\nNone.\n\n**Why:** `pressed_target` was stored as a `LayoutNodeId`. Mouse-down\non a Stateful widget (or anything whose POINTER_DOWN handler called\n`State::set`) marked the tree dirty → rebuild → slotmap key for the\npress target became stale → mouse-up's `dispatch_event_full` saw\n`stable_id(stale_id) = None` and dropped the release. Symptom:\n`on_click` closures never firing on widgets like `cn::button`,\n`cn::sidebar`, and the cn_demo Reset Animation button. Confirmed\nthis session by adding a `register stable=... event_types=[...]` log\nto `HandlerRegistry::register` and observing that handlers DID\nregister correctly — the failure was on the dispatch side, not the\nregistration side.\n\n**How to apply:**\n- New router state holding node identity across events: key by\n  `StableNodeId`, resolve to `LayoutNodeId` at emit time via\n  `tree.layout_id(stable)`.\n- Public router methods that previously took `LayoutNodeId`\n  (`is_pressed`, `pressed_target`, `on_unmount`, `on_mouse_leave`)\n  now either take/return `StableNodeId` or take a `\u0026RenderTree`\n  parameter to resolve.\n- `is_pressed(stable)` is keyed by stable id. Callers holding a\n  layout id should do `tree.stable_id(node).map(|s|\n  router.is_pressed(s))`.\n- `hovered`/`focused` are still `LayoutNodeId`-keyed (refreshed\n  every mouse_move, so the window of staleness is short and the\n  observed symptoms point only at click/drag for now). If\n  long-running hover/focus state ever shows similar drop-outs,\n  migrate them the same way.\n\n**Touch points:**\n- `crates/blinc_layout/src/event_router.rs` — fields + accessors +\n  on_mouse_{down,up,move,leave} + on_unmount\n- `crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/state.rs` — resolves\n  stable id before calling `router.is_pressed`\n- `crates/blinc_layout/src/renderer/stylesheet/selectors.rs` —\n  `router.pressed_target(self)` (takes tree)\n- `crates/blinc_app/src/{windowed,android,ios}.rs` — pass `tree` to\n  `on_mouse_leave`; use `has_pressed_target()` for `is_some` checks","files":null}]}